<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A translation maps <m>P({1},\,{4})</m> to <m>P'({6},\,{3})</m>.</p><p>(a) Find the translation vector <m>\mathbf{T}</m>.</p><div><m>\mathbf{T} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) The same translation maps a point Q to <m>Q'({-2},\,{-4})</m>. Find Q.</p><div>Q = ( <fillin characters="4" name="ans2"/> , <fillin characters="4" name="ans3"/> )  </div><div/></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) <m>\mathbf{T}</m> is the move from P to P': image minus object. Across: <m>{6} - {1} = {5}</m>; up: <m>{3} - {4} = {-1}</m>. So <m>\mathbf{T} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 5 \\ -1 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>(b) Q' is the image, so go back: <m>Q = Q' - \mathbf{T}</m>. Across: <m>{-2} - {5} = {-7}</m>; up: <m>{-4} - ({-1}) = {-3}</m>. So <m>Q({-7},\,{-3})</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} 5 \\ -1 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>-7</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>-3</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>